 "en": "<div><article> <div class=\"api-body\"> <section class=\"short-description\"> <p data-tid=\"b1\">Decorator that marks a class as a <a href=\"https://docs.nestjs.com/modules\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">module</a>.</p> <p><a href=\"#description\" data-tid=\"b0\">See more...</a></p> </section> <div class=\"overload-info\"> <pre class=\"language-typescript\"><code class=\"language-typescript\">\n <span class=\"member-name\">@<a href=\"#/api/common/Module\" class=\"code-anchor highlight\">Module</a></span>(metadata: <a href=\"https://api-references-nestjs.netlify.app/api/common/ModuleMetadata\" class=\"code-anchor highlight\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ModuleMetadata</a>)</code></pre> <h4 class=\"no-anchor\" id=\"parameters\" data-tid=\"b2\">Parameters</h4> <table class=\"is-full-width list-table parameters-table function-overload-parameters\"> <thead> <tr> <th data-tid=\"b3\">Option</th> <th data-tid=\"b4\">Type</th> <th data-tid=\"b5\">Description</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr class=\"function-overload-parameter\"> <td class=\"param-name\"> <code>metadata</code> </td> <td class=\"param-type\"><code><a href=\"https://api-references-nestjs.netlify.app/api/common/ModuleMetadata\" class=\"code-anchor highlight\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ModuleMetadata</a></code></td> <td class=\"param-description\"> <p data-tid=\"b6\">module configuration metadata</p> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h4 class=\"no-anchor\" id=\"returns\" data-tid=\"b7\">Returns</h4> <p><code>ClassDecorator</code></p> </div> <section class=\"see-also\"> <h3 id=\"see-also\" data-tid=\"b8\"><span>See also</span></h3> <ul> <li><p><a href=\"https://docs.nestjs.com/modules\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Modules</a></p> </li> </ul> </section> <section class=\"description\"> <h3 id=\"description\" data-tid=\"b9\"><span>Description</span></h3> <p data-tid=\"b10\">Modules are used by Nest to organize the application structure into scopes. Controllers and Providers are scoped by the module they are declared in. Modules and their classes (Controllers and Providers) form a graph that determines how Nest performs <a href=\"https://docs.nestjs.com/providers#dependency-injection\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Dependency Injection (DI)</a>.</p> </section> <section class=\"decorator-options\"> </section> </div> </article> </div>",
